  "notes": [
    {
      "at": [
        -20,
        29
      ],
      "id": 30,
      "text": "Timers, registers only: TIM2 makes a 1 kHz, 25 % PWM on PA0\ninto 10 kOhm / 1 uF, so V(RC) settles at 0.825 V; PA0 is\nwired back to PB6, where TIM4 captures the period and the\nLED on PB12 lights when it is 0.9-1.1 ms. TIM3 toggles PC13\nevery 10 ms; TIM1 gives complementary PWM on PA8 / PB13."
    }
  ],
